## 📌 Project Overview

**Mind Matters** is a student-led mental health awareness and peer-support campaign designed for first-year university students.

The project focuses on increasing awareness about mental health, reducing stigma around help-seeking, and connecting students with appropriate support resources.

The campaign combines **research, student surveys, awareness activities, peer-led workshops, resource mapping, and digital support through MindBridge**.

---

## 🎯 Core Focus

- Mental Health Awareness
- Stress & Anxiety Management
- Student Well-being
- Peer Support
- Help-Seeking Awareness
- Mental Health Resource Accessibility
- Digital Mental Wellness

---

## 💻 MindBridge

**MindBridge** is the digital component of the project, designed to provide students with an accessible and student-friendly mental-wellness platform.

The platform brings together mental-wellness resources, self-care tools, peer-support pathways, and information about professional support.

